Links between pages or sections, with the current one highlighted.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/navigation)

<%= embed UI::NavigationPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Navigation(aria_label: "Main", active_link: controller_name) do
  NavigationList do
    NavigationItem { NavigationLink(href: dashboard_path, value: "dashboard") { "Dashboard" } }
    NavigationItem { NavigationLink(href: projects_path, value: "projects") { "Projects" } }
    NavigationItem { NavigationLink(href: settings_path, active: current_page?(settings_path)) { "Settings" } }
  end
end
```

The root `<nav>` shares `variant:`, `size:` and `orientation:` with its links. Mark the current link either with
`active_link:` on the root and a matching `value:` on each link, or with `active: true` on the link itself (which
wins) - it's stamped `aria-current="page"`. The highlight is rendered on the server; there's no JavaScript. To swap
panels within a page use Tabs; for the trail to the current page use a [Breadcrumb](<%= page_path(:breadcrumb) %>).

